WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.143
Welcome to Group fifty eight

00:00:02.143 --> 00:00:10.100
Our project is the A I Driven Cyber Deception and Attack Detection Framework, guided
by Doctor Radhika G

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:15.992
This walkthrough uses actual interface screenshots and synthesized narration.

00:00:15.992 --> 00:00:23.812
This populated dashboard contains one thousand two hundred and twenty eight simulated
events

00:00:23.812 --> 00:00:30.017
These are illustrative presentation records, not real intercepted attacks

00:00:30.017 --> 00:00:32.567
S S H has four hundred and two

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:35.627
S Q L has three hundred and nineteen

00:00:35.627 --> 00:00:38.942
C I C D has two hundred and thirty nine

00:00:38.942 --> 00:00:42.682
The A I A P I has one hundred and sixty nine

00:00:42.682 --> 00:00:44.807
Web three has ninety nine

00:00:44.807 --> 00:00:49.567
Each total differs from every other by at least seventy.

00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:58.424
The full framework has five decoy designs: Shadow Shell, Oracle A I, Vault S Q L,
Ledger Trap and Forge C I

00:00:58.424 --> 00:01:07.033
The response engine checks static responses, then cached responses, then an A I
provider when configured

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:13.738
This simulated dataset does not contact the backend or create blockchain anchors.

00:01:13.738 --> 00:01:17.488
Now we switch to the separately verified live test

00:01:17.488 --> 00:01:22.138
We submitted a sample reconnaissance event using Try an attack

00:01:22.138 --> 00:01:27.838
The form sends command text to the backend; it does not execute that command

00:01:27.838 --> 00:01:36.163
The backend reported Logged, classified the intent as reconnaissance, and returned an
anchored on chain status.

00:01:36.163 --> 00:01:41.112
The matching event appeared in the live feed with an Anchored label

00:01:41.112 --> 00:01:51.675
The standard logging path uses keyword classification, Redis storage, a SHA two
hundred and fifty six hash, and a local Ganache test blockchain

00:01:51.675 --> 00:01:58.544
This test did not independently inspect a transaction receipt or exercise each network
decoy.

00:01:58.544 --> 00:02:04.748
After the test, the overview showed four events, with one reported anchored

00:02:04.748 --> 00:02:07.892
Older local records remained unchanged

00:02:07.892 --> 00:02:14.593
Ganache can reset when its hosted container restarts, and free services can sleep

00:02:14.593 --> 00:02:19.142
These limitations are documented on the project website

00:02:19.142 --> 00:02:28.077
The website also provides our team details, source repository, project document and
both demonstration views

00:02:28.077 --> 00:02:28.904
Thank you.
